# Jaguar Mark IX four-door saloon, 1958-1961.
#
# The last of the large separate-chassis Jaguar saloons: the Mark VIII body
# with a larger wrap-around rear window, a revised grille and bumper, disc
# brakes and the 3.8-litre six. A true level side elevation exists in the pack.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_IX
#
# Dimensions 4.99 x 1.91 x 1.60 m, wheelbase 3.05 m.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Pearl Grey and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes, recorded without
# claiming factory wording. Weights 4, 3, 2, 1, total 10, provisional pending
# the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Class 4.
# Dates 1958-1961 production, road tail staggered 1972-1974.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk9.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk9.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-mk9/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: grille bars, lamp internals, bumper overriders and wheel
# detail are simplified at sprite scale. The side view is a true elevation and
# governs the roofline, wing line and spats.


obj=citycar
